    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d695">

                <pb facs="0988" n="978" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg978"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/8–2245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-22T08:00:00+03:00">August 22, 1945—8
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 22—6:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3001. I reported my conversation with Molotov in a message to the Secretary via
                    Navy channels August 14<anchor n="28a" xml:id="d695-f1"/> in which Molotov
                    stated that Stalin did not now consider, for the reasons given in my message,
                        <pb facs="0989" n="979" xml:id="pg979"/> that there was any need for the
                    Soviet Government to give written confirmation of his verbal assurances to
                    support the Open Door policy, and I requested instructions. As I received no
                    reply to this message, I telegraphed again yesterday<anchor n="29"
                        xml:id="d695-f2"/> via Navy channel asking what decision had been reached. I
                    have had no further discussions with Molotov on this subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
